WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.240
Most people know that Apple MacBook laptops
are more expensive than many of the Windows

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.730
options, and a lot of Windows laptops pack
better performance specs while being cheaper

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.460
But for some reason, a lot of people are still
choosing to pay hundreds of dollars more for

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.269
a MacBook, so why is that?

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:18.120
And why have we seen so many Mac Users who
switched to good windows laptops because of

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.590
Apple’s high prices, go back after just
a few months?

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.400
If you’re not a fan of Apple devices, hold
on just a second before you dislike this video

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.331
and leave because chances are, there's probably
a few good reasons that you’ve never even

00:00:29.331 --> 00:00:30.331
thought about.

00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:34.360
Here are 18 reasons why MacBooks are so expensive,
let’s start off with the hardware.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.210
Most people who have used a MacBook trackpad
would agree that Apple’s force-touch trackpads

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.200
are by far, the best you can get.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.739
They don’t actually move or click, they
use a pane of glass with sensors underneath

00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:48.850
that sense pressure from your finger, and
the taptic engine below it vibrates to give

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.510
you haptic feedback that feels like a click
so with a perfect feel anywhere you press

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.630
and it can even sense pressure for 3D touch.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:01.390
These awesome trackpads cost much more than
the plastic ones with springs in other laptops.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.380
Apple also uses really fine-tuned high-quality
speakers that sound incredible and pack a

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.220
lot of volume for the size.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:18.110
Just listen to this comparison of Apple’s
2017 MacBook Pro and Dell’s newest 2019

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:28.570
XPS 13.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.580
As you’ve heard, the MacBook Pro’s speakers
sound much better in every way.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:39.060
And check out that same MacBook Pros microphone
quality compared to the new Dell XPS..

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.860
Yep, there’s a huge difference.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.430
And that’s something you can’t see on
a spec sheet.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:51.940
Apple also packs in additional custom chips
that weren’t cheap to develop, like Apple’s

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:57.299
T2 chip, which gives extra features like added
security through the secure enclave’s end-to-end

00:01:57.299 --> 00:02:02.650
encryption and things like HEVC encoding,
making a huge difference in encoding speed.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:06.189
Although the MacBook displays might not be
the highest resolution out there, Apple’s

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:09.030
MacBook displays are much brighter than the
average Windows laptop,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.440
and they also use very high-quality coatings
that reduce reflectivity by a lot, so they’re

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.030
much easier to use in bright conditions or
outside.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:21.410
MacBooks Pros are also incredibly color accurate,
supporting P3 wide-color gamut, which has

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.540
around 25% more colors compared to sRGB.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.640
One thing many don’t consider is that Apple’s
MacBooks are machined out of a solid block

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.540
of aluminum, which is not only expensive for
the materials alone but also more costly to

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.060
manufacture but result in a very solid chassis
that has a premium feel.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.870
Because of this, Apple was able to create
custom stacks of batteries that are sized

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:46.180
perfectly to fit the interior of the aluminum
chassis, so we get more battery life out of

00:02:46.180 --> 00:03:09.160
very thin laptops, but do cost more than standard
batteries.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:21.640
Every

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:26.980
single MacBook since 2013 packed top-of-the-line
SSD flash storage, while there are still some

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:32.519
Windows laptops to this day that come with
really slow physical hard drives, and if they

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:36.930
come with SSDs, many times, they’re nowhere
near as fast as Apple’s SSDs.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.680
On top of they give you options to spec up
to 4TB of extremely fast storage where many

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.790
windows laptops are limited to much less,
but admittedly the prices are really marked

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.570
up and you’ll end up with a crazy expensive
laptop.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:53.130
Apple’s MacBook Pros also feature more Thunderbolt
3 ports that you can get on Windows laptops.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:57.060
There are currently no Windows laptops that
we know of that have 4 full-speed Thunderbolt

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.629
3 ports like the 15” MacBook Pro does, and
that requires extra Thunderbolt chips from

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:02.629
Intel.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:05.740
Although not everyone likes Apple’s Touch
Bar, and personally we’re also not fans,

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.120
but they’re still incredibly high-quality
touch-screen OLED Displays, packing Touch

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:15.129
ID with end-to-end encryption which adds on
extra cost compared to windows laptops.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:17.379
Speaking of encryption, Let's move onto the
software.

00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:21.979
Apple focuses on privacy, making everything
on your MacBook as secure as possible, and

00:04:21.979 --> 00:04:25.590
they never sell any of your data like some
other companies do, so they have to earn their

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.509
full profit from the laptop itself.

00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:31.809
Apple’s macOS is only available on Apple
MacBooks, so that allows them to charge more

00:04:31.809 --> 00:04:35.669
for their laptops since if you need MacOS
there's no competition.

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:40.889
On the Windows laptop side there's many manufacturers
so they have to lower their prices to compete.

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:45.309
Since MacOS is only available on a small number
of machines, This limited number of components

00:04:45.309 --> 00:04:49.939
means that apps and drivers are very optimized
to make the most out hardware, because of

00:04:49.939 --> 00:04:54.309
this, software issues are less common and
old machines still run fast, which really

00:04:54.309 --> 00:04:58.080
improves resale value meaning Apple can charge
more for new ones.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.720
With MacOS you also get free major updates
every year, with a bunch of new features.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.779
Whereas, when a new version of Windows comes
out, you have to pay for it.

00:05:04.779 --> 00:05:09.680
Along with that, When you buy a MacBook you
get many work apps similar to Microsoft Word,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:10.809
powerpoint and excel.

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:14.340
Microsoft, on the other hand, charges for
all of those on top of your laptop purchases.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.340
You also don’t have to download additional
apps like PDF readers or video players that

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.340
can open a variety of formats, Apple supports
those files out of the box.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.680
It's nice to have these for free, including
any future updates but this does contribute

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.639
to higher base laptop prices.

00:05:20.639 --> 00:05:22.909
And finally, let’s touch on customer service.

00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:26.430
Apple is also the only laptop manufacturer
that has thousands of physical stores all

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.030
over the world, which makes it much easier
to get support or repairs.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.569
And they even have a no questions asked 14-day
return policy, without any return shipping

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:36.149
costs or other fees.

00:05:36.149 --> 00:05:40.960
Returns aren’t as easy with Windows laptops,
and a lot of them charge 15% restocking fees.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.740
Apple doesn’t do that, so they take the
loss themselves.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.689
There's no question that Apple laptops cost
a lot more money, but hopefully, this video

00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:51.680
helps you to see a few reasons why that price
is often higher than the competition.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.189
Judging off of the spec sheet, often times
we are shocked by what Apple charges for the

00:05:55.189 --> 00:06:00.150
base CPU and GPU spec, but once you compare
the hardware, software, and all of the little

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:04.050
details that you won’t see on the spec sheet,
it starts to make more sense.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.419
Of course, not everyone cares for these included
features, so a less expensive and more customizable

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:12.919
Windows Laptop still appeals to a lot of people
out there, and to them, the higher price of

00:06:12.919 --> 00:06:14.680
a MacBook is not worth it.

